{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"TDD contract card for 749c (authoritative contract: signed ticket plan + epic ACs). Preconditions: story claimed; S1 exposes undeclared/paths/none state; old empty-deps records use whole-HEAD freshness. Production paths: pure build_manifest/manifest reader contract; real temporary git+ticket store+SSHSIG verification into compute_validity; public current_material_fingerprint over ticket transitions; public resign_plan_review into signature verification. Tiers: unit contract tests for pure serialization/classification; integration tests with real git/store/signature where a lower mocked tier cannot prove authenticated-manifest authority or HEAD movement. Postconditions: none stays certified across unrelated HEAD drift; unscoped/legacy/malformed stay stale-head; plaintext tamper cannot forge none; scope/reason changes stale material; recovery re-sign authenticates none. Negative controls: paths preserve legacy bytes and dependency behavior; undeclared and future tokens remain fail-closed. Collateral invariants: legacy fingerprints and manifests remain byte-identical; other validity dimensions remain active. CI gate: exact nodes under make test, plus full make test. No fault-recovery contract applies. Every assertion observes return values, signed payloads, persisted ticket state, or serialized public contracts; no source grep/private-registry assertions."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785222357247088001,"uuid":"a26b4b33-3652-4c8c-9356-ff1fdd5cbedb"}